        <p>LADIES THIS FOR YOU TO READ. THERE IS NO PLACE LIKE HOME. And nothing in it looks more comfortable than a BRIGHT and CLEAN FIRESIDE. NO MORE BLACKLEADING REQUIRED. YOUR GRATES CLEANED IN FIVE MINUTES. . USE LAWSON'S BLACK. Sold in Tins at 20., 4d., 61d. each. Full directions for use on each tin. All you require to use it with is LAWSON'S PATENT BRUSH AND HOLDER, Price sp. One Brush will last a lifetime. The end of the Holder being attached to the Brush forms a Shield to prevent the lingers being soiled with the blank. LAWSON'S BLACK is a pleasure to use. No Brushing. No Dirt. Your Grates and Fenders will always look equal to new. Will not burn off or blister only where the bars ge red hot. SOLE MANUFACTURER FOR PATENTEE: M. M. LAWSON, BOOTLE, LIVERPOOL. A large size Tin, with Brush and Holder complete, free per Parcel Post for is. 4d. in stamps or postal order. Copy of unsolisited Testimonial, selected out of a number received. Hawthorne Villa, Linthorpe, Middlesbro'. Oct. 29, 1892. Mr- M. M. Lawson, Liverpool. DEAR SIR,—I have used some ot the "Lawson's Black" on my drawing and dining room fire grates, which my husband brought me to try, with the object of saving the servants the tedious work of blackleading, and I think it only right to comply with his desire to inform you that the trial has been most satisfactory in every respect; not only is the saving in time reduced more than three-fourths, and the appearance of the grates much improved as compared to blacklead, but the brush and holder you heve introduced en- ables those who use it to do so without in any way blacking or soiling their hands. I may also add that so far the appear- ance has not been affected by the heat of the fires.—Yours respectfully, JENNIE DOVE. Ask your Teaman, Grocer, or Chandler for it, And See that You Get It.</p>
