        <p>COUNTY COUItTBUSINESS. From the annual returns of the registrarB of County Courts, just issued by order of the House of Commons, we gather the following particulars of the large amount of business transacted during the past twelve months in the several courts in. this district. WARRINGTON.—In this court thrre were 4,519 plaints entered for trial, representing debts amounting to £10,934. Of these 2,897 were determined and judgment obtained for £5,581, exclusive of costs £403, and fees £1,728. The amount paid in to the credit of suitors was £5,965, and that paid out to them £5.970. There were 1,669 judgment summonses issued, 961 heard, 637 war- rants of commitment issued, 23 debtors imprisoned, 1,352 executions against goods issued, and eight sales made. RUNCORN.—In this court there were 1,220 plaints en- tered tor trial, with debts amounting to £3,227. Of these 746 were determined, and judgments obtained for £1,603, exclusive of costs £124, and fees £434. The amount paid into the credit of suitors was -£1,604, and that paid out to them £1,601. There were 169 judgment summonses issued, 104 heard, 63 warrants of commit- ment issued, five debtors imprisoned, 339 executions against goods, aid three sales made. Sr. HELENS AND WIDNES.—In this court there were 5.040 plaints entered for trial, with debts amounting t £13.166. Of these 3,541 were determined, and judg- ments ohtained for £7,742, exclusive of costa £367, and fees £2,179. The amount paid in to the credit of suitors was £7,620, and that paid to them £7,663. There were 2,556 judgment summonses issued, 1,479 heard. 847 warrants of commitment issued, 50 debtors imprisoned, 1,548 executions against goods, and seven sales made. IN ENGLAND AND WALES there were 1,068,693 plaints entered for trial (exclusive of the city of London), with debts amounting to £3,167,529. Of these 672,900 were determined, and judgments obtained for £1,643.825, ex- clusive of costs £146,073, and fees £427.468. The amount paid in to the credit of suitors was £1,628,081, and that paid out to them £1,629,264. There were 232,040 judgment summonses issued, • 141.868 heard, 78,952 warrants of commitment issued, 6,997 debtors imprisoned, 234,531 executions against goods, and 3,918 sales made.</p>
